    "cpsHistoryClearance": "<p>E&amp;E&nbsp;screen&nbsp;shots&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;active&nbsp;clearance&nbsp;document</p><p></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: yellow;\">Jordan&nbsp;Nicole&nbsp;Alleman&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;12/18/1997&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;216-51-0083&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Female&nbsp;White&nbsp;456058203</strong></p><p>Negative&nbsp;CPS&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Service&nbsp;Case&nbsp;hx.</p><p></p><p><strong><u>MD&nbsp;Judiciary:</u></strong></p><p>DV&nbsp;in&nbsp;June&nbsp;2026.</p><p>Negative&nbsp;NSOR.</p><p></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: yellow;\">Jeremy&nbsp;A&nbsp;Faber&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;09/22/2021&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;126-37-9206&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Male&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;White&nbsp;&nbsp;400834768</strong></p><p>Victim&nbsp;unsub&nbsp;neglect&nbsp;in&nbsp;Oct.&nbsp;2024&nbsp;(#241022887381).</p><p>Negative&nbsp;service&nbsp;case&nbsp;hx.</p><p></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: yellow;\">Jeffrey&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;Allen&nbsp;Faber&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;08/04/1997&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;212-51-0512&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Male&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;White&nbsp;&nbsp;487013488</strong></p><p>Maltreator&nbsp;unsub&nbsp;neglect&nbsp;in&nbsp;Oct.&nbsp;2024&nbsp;(#241022887381).</p><p>Negative&nbsp;service&nbsp;case&nbsp;hx.</p><p>Negative&nbsp;NSOR.</p><p></p><p><strong><u>MD&nbsp;Judiciary:</u></strong></p><p>Charged&nbsp;w/DRIVING&nbsp;VEH&nbsp;WHILE&nbsp;SO&nbsp;FAR&nbsp;IMPAIRED&nbsp;BY&nbsp;ALCOHOL&nbsp;CANNOT&nbsp;DRIVE&nbsp;SAFELY,&nbsp;DRIVING&nbsp;VEH.&nbsp;WHILE&nbsp;IMPAIRED&nbsp;BY&nbsp;ALCOHOL,&nbsp;DRIVING&nbsp;VEHICLE&nbsp;WHILE&nbsp;UNDER&nbsp;THE&nbsp;INFLUENCE&nbsp;OF&nbsp;ALCOHOL&nbsp;on&nbsp;6/22/26;&nbsp;court-no&nbsp;date&nbsp;yet&nbsp;<em>(resulted&nbsp;in&nbsp;accident)</em>:</p><p></p><p>Charged&nbsp;w/NEGLIGENT&nbsp;DRIVING&nbsp;VEHICLE&nbsp;IN&nbsp;CARELESS&nbsp;AND&nbsp;IMPRUDENT&nbsp;MANNER&nbsp;ENDANGERING&nbsp;PROPERTY,&nbsp;LIFE&nbsp;AND&nbsp;PERSON,&nbsp;DRIVING&nbsp;VEH.&nbsp;WHILE&nbsp;IMPAIRED&nbsp;BY&nbsp;ALCOHOL,&nbsp;DRIVING&nbsp;VEHICLE&nbsp;WHILE&nbsp;UNDER&nbsp;THE&nbsp;INFLUENCE&nbsp;OF&nbsp;ALCOHOL&nbsp;PER&nbsp;SE,&nbsp;DRIVING&nbsp;VEHICLE&nbsp;WHILE&nbsp;UNDER&nbsp;THE&nbsp;INFLUENCE&nbsp;OF&nbsp;ALCOHOL&nbsp;on&nbsp;3/14/26;&nbsp;court&nbsp;6/30/26;</p><p></p><p>Stet&nbsp;violate&nbsp;prot&nbsp;order&nbsp;in&nbsp;Jan.&nbsp;2025;</p><p>DV&nbsp;in&nbsp;June&nbsp;2024.</p><p></p><p></p><p><strong>Oct.&nbsp;2024&nbsp;(#241022887381)&nbsp;-</strong>&nbsp;Jeffrey&nbsp;Faber&nbsp;was&nbsp;at&nbsp;his&nbsp;brother&#39;s&nbsp;apartment&nbsp;complex.&nbsp;Jeremy&nbsp;was&nbsp;asleep&nbsp;when&nbsp;he&nbsp;was&nbsp;carried&nbsp;by&nbsp;his&nbsp;father&nbsp;down&nbsp;to&nbsp;his&nbsp;father&#39;s&nbsp;truck.&nbsp;Mr.&nbsp;Faber&nbsp;did&nbsp;consume&nbsp;alcohol;&nbsp;there&nbsp;were&nbsp;4&nbsp;cans&nbsp;observed&nbsp;in&nbsp;his&nbsp;truck.&nbsp;It&nbsp;took&nbsp;multiple&nbsp;attempts&nbsp;to&nbsp;wake&nbsp;up&nbsp;Mr.&nbsp;Faber,&nbsp;the&nbsp;detective&nbsp;shined&nbsp;his&nbsp;light&nbsp;in&nbsp;his&nbsp;eyes,&nbsp;tapping&nbsp;on&nbsp;his&nbsp;shoulder,&nbsp;turned&nbsp;on&nbsp;his&nbsp;sirens&nbsp;and&nbsp;cruiser&nbsp;lights.&nbsp;It&nbsp;took&nbsp;approximately&nbsp;15&nbsp;minutes&nbsp;to&nbsp;wake&nbsp;up&nbsp;Mr.&nbsp;Faber.&nbsp;Mr.&nbsp;Faber&nbsp;had&nbsp;no&nbsp;idea&nbsp;what&nbsp;was&nbsp;going&nbsp;on&nbsp;due&nbsp;to&nbsp;his&nbsp;intoxication.&nbsp;The&nbsp;concern&nbsp;is&nbsp;that&nbsp;the&nbsp;apartment&nbsp;complex&nbsp;has&nbsp;a&nbsp;pond&nbsp;and&nbsp;is&nbsp;next&nbsp;to&nbsp;a&nbsp;busy&nbsp;road&nbsp;and&nbsp;how&nbsp;difficult&nbsp;it&nbsp;was&nbsp;to&nbsp;wake&nbsp;Mr.&nbsp;Faber.&nbsp;LDSS&nbsp;issuing&nbsp;an&nbsp;Unsubstantiated&nbsp;finding&nbsp;that&nbsp;appears&nbsp;most&nbsp;appropriate&nbsp;currently.&nbsp;Mr.&nbsp;Faber&nbsp;did&nbsp;place&nbsp;his&nbsp;son&nbsp;at&nbsp;risk&nbsp;of&nbsp;harm&nbsp;while&nbsp;being&nbsp;under&nbsp;the&nbsp;influence&nbsp;of&nbsp;so&nbsp;much&nbsp;alcohol&nbsp;that&nbsp;law&nbsp;enforcement&nbsp;was&nbsp;unable&nbsp;to&nbsp;wake&nbsp;him&nbsp;up&nbsp;after&nbsp;multiple&nbsp;attempts.&nbsp;His&nbsp;son&nbsp;was&nbsp;asleep&nbsp;on&nbsp;his&nbsp;lap;&nbsp;he&nbsp;thankfully&nbsp;did&nbsp;not&nbsp;leave&nbsp;the&nbsp;vehicle&nbsp;despite&nbsp;the&nbsp;driver’s&nbsp;door&nbsp;being&nbsp;open.&nbsp;The&nbsp;child&nbsp;was&nbsp;not&nbsp;harmed&nbsp;in&nbsp;any&nbsp;way&nbsp;but&nbsp;there&nbsp;was&nbsp;risk.&nbsp;The&nbsp;child&nbsp;could&nbsp;have&nbsp;walked&nbsp;away&nbsp;from&nbsp;the&nbsp;vehicle&nbsp;and&nbsp;been&nbsp;hit&nbsp;by&nbsp;a&nbsp;vehicle&nbsp;either&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;parking&nbsp;lot&nbsp;or&nbsp;the&nbsp;busy&nbsp;road&nbsp;next&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;complex&nbsp;or&nbsp;fallen&nbsp;into&nbsp;the&nbsp;nearby&nbsp;pond.&nbsp;Those&nbsp;things&nbsp;did&nbsp;not&nbsp;occur,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;child&nbsp;did&nbsp;not&nbsp;even&nbsp;appear&nbsp;to&nbsp;understand&nbsp;what&nbsp;was&nbsp;happening.</p>",
